# File Handling + JSON 📁

today i combined file handling
with JSON because they go together
especially in AI projects

---

## File Handling (quick recap)
with open("file.txt", "w") as f:
    f.write("hello ganesh")

with open("file.txt", "r") as f:
    print(f.read())

## modes i use most:
"r"  → read
"w"  → write (overwrites!)
"a"  → append (adds to end)

---

## JSON (this is important!)
JSON = JavaScript Object Notation
basically python dictionary
but used everywhere in APIs

import json

## dict to json string
data = {"name": "ganesh", "age": 21}
json_string = json.dumps(data)
print(json_string)

## save json to file
with open("data.json", "w") as f:
    json.dump(data, f, indent=4)

## read json from file
with open("data.json", "r") as f:
    loaded = json.load(f)
    print(loaded["name"])  # ganesh

## why JSON matters:
→ APIs return JSON responses
→ AI models save configs in JSON
→ used everywhere in web dev
→ very important to know!
